Mr. Croft -

Thanks for the note. Confirming a few items on your existing
marine policy (Eileen C, policy on file, renewal mid-January 2027).

  1. Your standard policy covers the vessel during routine yard
     maintenance windows of up to seven (7) consecutive days at a
     scheduled USCG-recognized yard. Rockland Marine Yard
     qualifies.

  2. The Wednesday Dec 9 through Friday Dec 11 window (three
     days) sits comfortably within that coverage. No additional
     rider needed.

  3. Coverage during sea trial: the standard policy treats sea
     trials within Penobscot Bay as ordinary in-service use.
     Routine. No additional rider needed.

  4. If the yard pushes the splash past Dec 16 for any reason
     (parts delay, weather, etc.), the seven-day window will be
     exceeded and we'd want to issue a no-cost extension rider.
     Just call if that happens.

Renewal materials for the 2027 policy will mail mid-January as
usual.

